@startuml
title ClinicBook - Fioralba Zika domain model (cancellation and daily schedule)

skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
skinparam classFontSize 12
skinparam noteFontSize 10
skinparam linetype ortho

' Source of truth: docs/REQUIREMENTS.md and docs/USER_STORIES.md on develop.
' FR-02, FR-03, FR-04, FR-05, FR-06, FR-07, FR-09 and FR-17 are referenced.
' FR-16 is "Could" and is deliberately not modelled as a lifecycle change here.

abstract class User {
  #id : int
  #name : string
}

class Patient extends User {
  +registered : bool = true
  +futureBookedCount(now : DateTime) : int
  +noShowsLast90Days(now : DateTime) : int
  +hasOverlappingBooked(now : DateTime) : bool
}

class Receptionist extends User {
}

class Doctor extends User {
  +viewDailySchedule(day : Date) : DailyScheduleEntry[]
}

class Appointment {
  +id : int
  +start : DateTime
  +durationMinutes : int = 20
  +status : AppointmentStatus
  +isFuture(now : DateTime) : bool
  +belongsTo(patient : Patient) : bool
  +cancel(actor : User, now : DateTime) : void
}

enum AppointmentStatus {
  BOOKED
  CANCELLED
}

class TimeSlot {
  +start : DateTime
  +end : DateTime
  +durationMinutes : int = 20
  +isWithinClinicHours() : bool
}

class BlockedPeriod {
  +id : int
  +start : DateTime
  +end : DateTime
}

class DailyScheduleEntry <<derived>> {
  +time : DateTime
  +patientName : string
  +status : AppointmentStatus
}

' Associations
User <|-- Patient
User <|-- Receptionist
User <|-- Doctor

Patient "1" <-- "0..*" Appointment : patient
Doctor "1" <-- "0..*" Appointment : doctor
TimeSlot "1" <-- "0..1" Appointment : occupies
Doctor "1" --> "0..*" BlockedPeriod : blocks
Doctor "1" ..> "0..*" DailyScheduleEntry : derives
DailyScheduleEntry "0..*" ..> "1" Appointment : from
Appointment --> AppointmentStatus

note right of Appointment
  Status BOOKED is the active booking.
  Status CANCELLED is retained history and releases the slot.
  cancel needs: status BOOKED, start in the future, and either
  owner patient at least 24 h before start, or any receptionist
  before start (FR-06, US-08, US-09).
end note

note bottom of Patient
  Lifetime association to Appointment is 0..* because records are kept.
  Future active bookings are the subset with status BOOKED and start later than now.
  FR-05 constraint: that subset has at most 2 members, checked on each booking.
  Cancelled appointments do not count (proposed acceptance rule).
  FR-17: a patient may not hold overlapping BOOKED appointments (Should).
end note

note right of Patient
  FR-09 (Should): 3 no-shows in the last 90 days allow booking only through reception.
  The source of no-show records is not defined in the shared documents (open question).
end note

note left of TimeSlot
  Slots are 20 minutes, 08:00-16:00, Monday to Friday (FR-02).
  A slot is free only if future, not blocked, and without a BOOKED appointment.
  FR-04: at most one BOOKED appointment per doctor and start time.
end note

note right of BlockedPeriod
  A slot inside a blocked period is not offered as free
  (booking structured specification).
end note

note bottom of Doctor
  FR-07: view own non-cancelled appointments for a chosen day,
  in chronological order. Each entry shows time, patient name and status.
end note

@enduml
